  "title": "Mambo, Neighbour! Greetings at the Gate",
  "category": "social",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "level": 1,
  "order": 103,
  "theme": "greetings",
  "culturalNote": "Kenyans greet before anything else — skipping the greeting and jumping straight to business comes across as rude. Who you greet decides how you greet: an older woman like your neighbour gets the polite \"Habari ya asubuhi?\" (and \"mama\" as a sign of respect), while her teenage son gets a casual \"Mambo?\" or \"Niaje?\". Women are often called by their first child's name — \"Mama Njeri\" is \"Njeri's mum\". You are John again, newly moved into a flat in Kilimani.",
  "startingPoint": "It's 7:30 on your first morning in the new flat. Mama Njeri from next door greets you at the gate.",
  "grammarFocus": [
    "greetings",
    "ko-location",
    "present-na"
  ],
